  {
   "entity": "quest",
   "slot": "create",
   "srcId": "sg509_fire",
   "phase": 2,
   "name": "At the Salvager's Fire",
   "data": {
    "name": "At the Salvager's Fire",
    "description": "The salvager's fire still burns below the Wreck. Sit with her and ask about getting aboard, the charts, the chests, the deep, the Haul, trading or the watch log.",
    "image": "https://uploadthing.b-cdn.net/f/630cf6e7-c152-4dea-a3ff-821de76d7f5a_default.webp",
    "questType": "event",
    "questRank": "D",
    "successDescription": "The fire's there when you need it.",
    "retryDelay": "none",
    "attemptDelay": "none",
    "consecutiveObjectives": true,
    "hidden": true,
    "requiredLevel": 1,
    "maxLevel": 100,
    "maxAttempts": 100,
    "maxCompletes": 100,
    "prerequisiteQuestId": null,
    "tierLevel": null,
    "requiredVillage": null,
    "requiredBloodlineId": null,
    "startsAt": null,
    "endsAt": null,
    "content": {
     "objectives": [
      {
       "id": "d_open",
       "task": "dialog",
       "description": "The Ghost Ship hung over this coast longer than anyone's grandmother could remember. Now she has come down.<br><br>A salvager mends a net by a driftwood fire below the wreck. \"Another one come to pick her bones. Sit, then. Ask.\"",
       "sceneBackground": "rX78pJPETsUL2JrsSvGHn",
       "sceneCharacters": [
        "Xugt7415D3-tepLfxpwM5"
       ],
       "nextObjectiveId": [
        {
         "text": "Sit by the fire",
         "nextObjectiveId": "d_menu"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "id": "d_menu",
       "task": "dialog",
       "description": "She nods at a board of driftwood where she pins what the sea gives back. \"Ask what you came to ask.\"<br><br><i>Pick a topic. You can come back to this board after each answer.</i>",
       "sceneBackground": "@scene:sg509_board_menu",
       "sceneCharacters": [
        "Xugt7415D3-tepLfxpwM5"
       ],
       "nextObjectiveId": [
        {
         "text": "How do I get aboard her?",
         "nextObjectiveId": "a_threes"
        },
        {
         "text": "What are these charts?",
         "nextObjectiveId": "c_once"
        },
        {
         "text": "What's in the chests?",
         "nextObjectiveId": "x_chests"
        },
        {
         "text": "What's down in the deep?",
         "nextObjectiveId": "p_seals"
        },
        {
         "text": "What's the Haul?",
         "nextObjectiveId": "h_haul"
        },
        {
         "text": "Can I trade what I find?",
         "nextObjectiveId": "t_trade"
        },
        {
         "text": "What's the watch log?",
         "nextObjectiveId": "w_board"
        },
        {
         "text": "That's all for now",
         "nextObjectiveId": "z_bye"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "id": "a_threes",
       "task": "dialog",
       "description": "\"Nobody goes aboard alone and comes back. Go in threes.\"<br><br><i>She is ashore Friday to Sunday, every weekend. The Wreck is a party dungeon in sector 210. It takes exactly 3 players, and a run lasts up to an hour.</i>",
       "sceneBackground": "@scene:sg509_board_threes",
       "sceneCharacters": [
        "Xugt7415D3-tepLfxpwM5"
       ],
       "nextObjectiveId": [
        {
         "text": "Which part of her?",
         "nextObjectiveId": "a_hulls"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "id": "a_hulls",
       "task": "dialog",
       "description": "\"She broke in two. The near half is faded and gentler. The far half still remembers every order.\"<br><br><i>The Faded Skyglass Wreck (sector 210, 16/6) opens at level 30. The Skyglass Wreck (15/6) is the endgame hull and opens at level 80.</i>",
       "sceneBackground": "@scene:sg509_board_hulls",
       "sceneCharacters": [
        "Xugt7415D3-tepLfxpwM5"
       ],
       "nextObjectiveId": [
        {
         "text": "What comes back out?",
         "nextObjectiveId": "a_loot"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "id": "a_loot",
       "task": "dialog",
       "description": "\"Coin, stores and paper. <b>Charts</b>, wet ones, drawn by the crew themselves.\"<br><br><i>Every clear pays ryo and EXP and can drop charts. The endgame hull also drops the rarer charts, ledger pages, the Lantern and a shard.</i>",
       "sceneBackground": "@scene:sg509_board_loot",
       "sceneCharacters": [
        "Xugt7415D3-tepLfxpwM5"
       ],
       "nextObjectiveId": [
        {
         "text": "Ask something else",
         "nextObjectiveId": "r_menu"
        },
        {
         "text": "That's all for now",
         "nextObjectiveId": "z_bye"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "id": "c_once",
       "task": "dialog",
       "description": "\"Each chart is the way into one corner of her, and she doesn't hold still, so it's good once.\"<br><br><i>Take a chart to the <b>Battle Arena</b> and run it alone; claim any waiting reward first. The chart is spent when the run starts. Health and chakra carry from fight to fight, and a lost fight ends the run.</i>",
       "sceneBackground": "@scene:sg509_board_once",
       "sceneCharacters": [
        "Xugt7415D3-tepLfxpwM5"
       ],
       "nextObjectiveId": [
        {
         "text": "Where do they lead?",
         "nextObjectiveId": "c_ladder"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "id": "c_ladder",
       "task": "dialog",
       "description": "\"The low-tide charts and the rosters take you to the lower decks. Down there are the crew's own charts: what they buried, the works, the archive, the helm. Those lead to the places the crew sealed shut.\"<br><br><i>Most runs can drop the next chart down. The Captain's Watch chart comes only from the endgame Wreck or an Archive Chart Case.</i>",
       "sceneBackground": "@scene:sg509_board_ladder",
       "sceneCharacters": [
        "Xugt7415D3-tepLfxpwM5"
       ],
       "nextObjectiveId": [
        {
         "text": "What do I get for winning?",
         "nextObjectiveId": "c_pick"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "id": "c_pick",
       "task": "dialog",
       "description": "\"Win, and the crew lets you choose what to carry out.\"<br><br><i>A winning ending lets you pick one reward from a short list and pays EXP. Some runs end in a last room: leave with what you hold, or press on for more and keep only that if you lose. Any other loss pays nothing. Every chart shows its difficulty in stars.</i>",
       "sceneBackground": "@scene:sg509_board_pick",
       "sceneCharacters": [
        "Xugt7415D3-tepLfxpwM5"
       ],
       "nextObjectiveId": [
        {
         "text": "Ask something else",
         "nextObjectiveId": "r_menu"
        },
        {
         "text": "That's all for now",
         "nextObjectiveId": "z_bye"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "id": "x_chests",
       "task": "dialog",
       "description": "\"The crew sealed their crates well. Prying them open is half the fun.\"<br><br><i>A <b>Skyglass Coffer</b> holds Filament, Serum, a Crown Fragment or, rarely, the Skyglass Katana. A <b>Sealed Treasury</b> holds ryo, Imperial Gold, Rare Jewels and Unobtanium. <b>Crown's Hoard</b> holds a Coffer, a Treasury and a Skyglass Token. <b>Unmarked Cargo</b> could be anything.</i>",
       "sceneBackground": "@scene:sg511_board_chests",
       "sceneCharacters": [
        "Xugt7415D3-tepLfxpwM5"
       ],
       "nextObjectiveId": [
        {
         "text": "And the supplies?",
         "nextObjectiveId": "x_supplies"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "id": "x_supplies",
       "task": "dialog",
       "description": "\"Pills, kunai, dried fish. They ate better than we do.\"<br><br><i>Medicine Inro: healing and chakra pills. Sage's Strongbox: battle potions and rarer pills. Elemental Tool Pouch: Elemental Kunai and tools. Galley Stores: 2,000 EXP for an eligible active pet. Little Horror's Jar, a rare drop from the endgame Wreck, is the event's pet.</i>",
       "sceneBackground": "@scene:sg511_board_supplies",
       "sceneCharacters": [
        "Xugt7415D3-tepLfxpwM5"
       ],
       "nextObjectiveId": [
        {
         "text": "And the glass?",
         "nextObjectiveId": "x_craft"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "id": "x_craft",
       "task": "dialog",
       "description": "\"The glass itself is worth more than anything they packed, if you know how to work it.\"<br><br><i>12 Skyglass Filament craft a Skyglass Crystal, and 5 Fragments of the Skyglass Crown craft <b>The Skyglass Crown</b>. Both need a crafting rank; without one, trade them to someone who has it.</i>",
       "sceneBackground": "@scene:sg511_board_craft",
       "sceneCharacters": [
        "Xugt7415D3-tepLfxpwM5"
       ],
       "nextObjectiveId": [
        {
         "text": "Ask something else",
         "nextObjectiveId": "r_menu"
        },
        {
         "text": "That's all for now",
         "nextObjectiveId": "z_bye"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "id": "p_seals",
       "task": "dialog",
       "description": "\"Some doors the crew sealed. The Reliquary Seal opens the reliquary. The Last Heading takes you back to the night she fell.\"<br><br><i>These are the Epic runs, The Sealed Reliquary and The Fall. Their charts drop from the Archive and the Captain's Watch.</i>",
       "sceneBackground": "@scene:sg509_board_seals",
       "sceneCharacters": [
        "Xugt7415D3-tepLfxpwM5"
       ],
       "nextObjectiveId": [
        {
         "text": "And the rot?",
         "nextObjectiveId": "p_rot"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "id": "p_rot",
       "task": "dialog",
       "description": "\"Soak a sealed chart in <b>Core Rot</b> and the rot remembers the place worse.\"<br><br><i>Use an Epic chart from your inventory with 3 Core Rot, then win one fight. You get the tainted chart: a harder run where you pick 2 rewards. Lose, and the chart comes back but the Rot is spent. Core Rot drops from the endgame Wreck, the low-tide runs, The Fall and the tainted runs.</i>",
       "sceneBackground": "@scene:sg509_board_rot",
       "sceneCharacters": [
        "Xugt7415D3-tepLfxpwM5"
       ],
       "nextObjectiveId": [
        {
         "text": "And past that?",
         "nextObjectiveId": "p_lantern"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "id": "p_lantern",
       "task": "dialog",
       "description": "\"Some come back from the deep with a <b>lantern</b> that won't go out. It points at the mountain, at <b>Crownhold</b>, the castle she sailed from. Someone still gives orders there.\"<br><br><i>A Lastlight Lantern opens Crownhold. It drops from the Epic and tainted runs, and rarely from the endgame Wreck.</i>",
       "sceneBackground": "@scene:sg509_board_lantern",
       "sceneCharacters": [
        "Xugt7415D3-tepLfxpwM5"
       ],
       "nextObjectiveId": [
        {
         "text": "Ask something else",
         "nextObjectiveId": "r_menu"
        },
        {
         "text": "That's all for now",
         "nextObjectiveId": "z_bye"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "id": "h_haul",
       "task": "dialog",
       "description": "\"Some bring back a ledger page or a stores list and go after holds no chart shows. They come back heavy, or not at all.\"<br><br><i>A page opens The Haul: up to 5 steps of crate, locker or cut through. Deeper, bigger chests of profession materials. Leave after any step to keep them; lose a fight and you keep nothing. Pages drop from the endgame Wreck and the Rare runs.</i>",
       "sceneBackground": "@scene:sg509_board_haul",
       "sceneCharacters": [
        "Xugt7415D3-tepLfxpwM5"
       ],
       "nextObjectiveId": [
        {
         "text": "Ask something else",
         "nextObjectiveId": "r_menu"
        },
        {
         "text": "That's all for now",
         "nextObjectiveId": "z_bye"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "id": "t_trade",
       "task": "dialog",
       "description": "\"What you can't use, trade. Every chart and every shard has a buyer.\"<br><br><i>Charts, Core Rot, Haul pages, shards and Skyglass Tokens can be traded. Crown's Hoard, Unmarked Cargo, the Haul's chests and some once-only rewards cannot.</i>",
       "sceneBackground": "@scene:sg509_board_trade",
       "sceneCharacters": [
        "Xugt7415D3-tepLfxpwM5"
       ],
       "nextObjectiveId": [
        {
         "text": "What's a Skyglass Token?",
         "nextObjectiveId": "t_token"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "id": "t_token",
       "task": "dialog",
       "description": "\"The crew's colours still take to steel.\"<br><br><i>A Skyglass Token unlocks one Skyglass skin, once, on a weapon you already own: Aetherion, Thornsilver, Night's Testament, Stormrender, Oathbinder, Ink of the Void, The Unwritten, Gaea's Embrace, Warden's Bracers, Eclipsed Dawnblade, Zephyr's Whisper or Yuki's Frostbite. A boss's own token unlocks that boss's skin.</i>",
       "sceneBackground": "@scene:sg509_board_token",
       "sceneCharacters": [
        "Xugt7415D3-tepLfxpwM5"
       ],
       "nextObjectiveId": [
        {
         "text": "Ask something else",
         "nextObjectiveId": "r_menu"
        },
        {
         "text": "That's all for now",
         "nextObjectiveId": "z_bye"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "id": "w_board",
       "task": "dialog",
       "description": "\"I keep their <b>watch log</b>. It washes up a page at a time. I dry one each weekend and pin it up in the <b>Administration Building</b>.\"<br><br><i>A new page goes up each weekend in your village's Administration Building; Wake Island has one too, nearest the Wreck. Take it first: only what you do while you carry it counts.</i>",
       "sceneBackground": "@scene:sg509_board_logboard",
       "sceneCharacters": [
        "Xugt7415D3-tepLfxpwM5"
       ],
       "nextObjectiveId": [
        {
         "text": "What's on a page?",
         "nextObjectiveId": "w_orders"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "id": "w_orders",
       "task": "dialog",
       "description": "\"One watch's orders. Lately the name at the top isn't one of theirs.\"<br><br><i>Do the orders in any order and claim each reward from your Logbook. Finish them all for the page's last reward. The page closes Tuesday 00:00 UTC (Monday 6 PM Central).</i>",
